2026-07-23T09:31:31.142-05:00	feedback	row=0011	actual_labels.jsonl	reviewer_note	No tests to handle already existent MRNs. Furthermore there is no functional test to confirm the presence of the conflicting MRN message upon rejection.  Additional notes: Is MRN the only field that gates patient registration? Consider, what if all the same patient information but the MRN is unique? Is that allowed? Could be unforeseen edge case.	by=dsobc
2026-07-23T09:31:31.142-05:00	feedback	row=0012	actual_labels.jsonl	reviewer_note	To properly test this requirement, there needs to be a consideration that the sepsis alert is triggered iff: - A) heart rate > 90 bpm - B) temperature > 38.0 celsius - both A) and B) both occurred within a 4-hour window  Thus, there should be negative tests to confirm: - no sepsis alert occurs if only heart heart is exceeded - no sepsis alert occurs if only temperature is exceeded - no sepsis alert if heart is exceeded and then at 4 hours + 1 minute (depends on detectability limits as this could be even at the seconds level potentially)   Edge cases:  - no testing around the exact limit of 4 hours. - detectability of the temperature/heart rate is unclear - if the temperature exceeds for a very brief time (say 0.5 seconds), does that count? is there a minimum length of time the temperature / bpm needs to be sustained at that high level in order for the system to record it; otherwise, there could be blips in these values that result in false positives OR if the system is unable to detect at the desired rate, there could be false negatives related to alert reporting.	by=dsobc
2026-07-23T09:31:31.143-05:00	feedback	row=0013	actual_labels.jsonl	reviewer_note	This requirement contains several sub-requirements:  - The system SHALL allow a provider to place a laboratory order - The system SHALL allow selection of a collection priority of STAT  - The system SHALL allow selection of a collection priority of Routine - The system SHALL print a specimen label containing the patient's MRN - The system SHALL print a specimen label containing the laboratory order ID.  However, the tests only cover:   Positive test: Verify a provider can place a laboratory order with a STAT  Negative test (general): Verify a laboratory order cannot be signed without a collection priority selected.  There are additional negative/positive tests that apply based on the different sub-requirements identified.	by=dsobc
2026-07-23T09:31:31.143-05:00	feedback	row=0014	actual_labels.jsonl	reviewer_note	This requirement looks to specifically test a unique scenario where a patient with an infection control entry is displayed with a banner. The tests do not match the terminology used (should be "Isolation Precautions") not quarantine.  It is acceptable to state that negative tests are "N-A" because It is clarified in the requirement "Context:" that non-active contact isolation orders patients is covered elsewhere (e.g., in a different requirement).	by=dsobc
